          "filename": "Backyard view of the Old fort in Zanzibar.jpg",
          "caption": "The Old Fort’s foundation was laid by the Portuguese in early 1710s but the building was finalized in a Omani style in 1780. Was later used both as a prison by the British officials until 1950, and also as a railway workshop in the 1920s when the railway from Bububu to town was built. Now it is used as a cultural centre of Stone Town.",
